# Upstream's own ignore conventions, kept verbatim. Nothing above this line is
# ours, and nothing below it removes an upstream entry to make room for a
# fork-owned one.
#
# SQLite's release archives ship no `.gitignore` at all -- neither
# sqlite-amalgamation-3530400.zip nor sqlite-src-3530400.zip carries one, and
# the Fossil repository's own exclusions live in `.fossil-settings/ignore-glob`
# and `.fossil-settings/binary-glob`, files this tree does not vendor. The
# entries in the first block are therefore upstream's *build products* rather
# than upstream's ignore file, and they are listed so a build made with upstream's
# own makefile -- a `configure && make` in a sibling directory, which
# upstream/README.md describes -- cannot commit a stray object.
#
# `upstream/main.mk:1554-1563` is what installs the shared library, so the shared
# object names are here; `upstream/main.mk:1613-1614` is what installs the two
# headers.
#
# One rule governs this block, and it is why the database patterns carry a
# leading slash: a `.gitignore` pattern with no slash matches at *any* depth, so
# an unanchored `*.db` would swallow the ten `fuzzdata*.db` and
# `dbfuzz2-seed1.db` inputs under `test/` that upstream's own tests read, and
# unanchored `*.def` would swallow `upstream/auto.def`. Anchored to the top
# directory, they name what running a shell in this checkout produces and
# nothing that upstream ships. No other pattern in this block matches any
# vendored file.
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.dmp
*.swp
/*.db
/*.db-journal
/*.db-wal
/*.db-shm
/*.sqlite
/*.sqlite3

# zig build artefacts (fork addition).
#
# These are directories rather than single files because a normal `zig build`
# creates them, and a normal `zig build` must not dirty the tree or leak into
# the package published from it. None of them is named in build.zig.zon
# `.paths`, so an ignored directory can never become part of the package.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
# Zig 0.17 stores fetched dependencies in this package-local directory.
zig-pkg/

# The upstream test suite is never ignored. Nothing under test/ is build output,
# and dropping any of it would leave a tree that cannot run the suite upstream
# ships. There is no blanket `!test/` re-inclusion here because the rules above
# are already narrow enough that none of them reaches into test/; adding one
# would be a second mechanism guarding the same thing, and a reader would have
# to work out which of the two was load-bearing.

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own cache and
# output tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so a build
# run from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/

# Nix and devenv working-tree artefacts (fork addition).
#
# `nix build` writes `result` (and `result-1`, `result-2`, ... on a rebuild)
# into the directory that asked for it, and `devenv` writes its resolved
# inputs and its state beside the project. None of them is named in
# build.zig.zon `.paths`, so an ignored path can never become part of the
# package either. `devenv.lock` and `flake.lock` are deliberately *not* here:
# they are real inputs, they belong to the driver, and ignoring them would be
# the wrong way to keep a build out of a commit.
result
result-*
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.devenv.flakes/
devenv.local.nix
.direnv/